# Series for the Sovereign integration build.
#
# Each non-empty, non-comment line names a topic branch, typically
# `topic/<short-name>`. For every listed topic there must also be a
# corresponding `topic-base/<short-name>` branch. The range
# `topic-base/<short-name>..topic/<short-name>` is the topic's patch;
# `compose.sh` applies those ranges, in this order, on top of the
# upstream base named in `sovereign/upstream-base` to produce the
# derived `sovereign/integration` ref.
#
# Adding a line ≈ merging a PR. Removing a line ≈ reverting one.
# Reordering lines reorders application; topic branches *should* be
# usually independent (commute), but the order is semantically real:
# a later topic may depend on effects introduced by earlier topics.
# When a topic no longer applies cleanly, the canary writes
# `topic-repair-base/<short-name>` at the freshly composed prefix to
# rebase that one topic onto; `topic-base/<short-name>` moves only
# after that topic has been successfully rewritten.
#
# `compose.sh --develop` also applies any `topic/*` branch not listed
# here, ordered by first-commit date, on top of the integration. That
# is the local-dev "see your in-flight work in context" view; CI never
# uses it.

topic/product-quality-update-url
topic/linux-archive-auto-update
